 <div class="card"><h3>What does “Voice style” (Balanced, Stable, Creative) do in Dub Long Video?</h3><p>At the price step you can choose how the voice speaks. <strong>Balanced</strong> (the default) is the usual natural mix and suits most videos. <strong>Stable</strong> is calmer and more even from line to line and follows your text closely, with less emotion; it suits news, narration, courtrooms and lectures. <strong>Creative</strong> is more lively and varied, with a wider range of feeling but less predictable; it suits drama, stories and animation. It never changes the words or the price, and it also applies to later corrections of that dub. Listen to the result before you publish it.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><h3>What are credits and how are costs calculated?</h3><p>Credits are how you pay on Lisan AI: 1 credit = $0.01 USD (100 credits = $1.00). The cost depends on how much text and audio you process. Every button shows its estimated cost before you click it, and actual usage appears in the green box in Step 1.</p></div>
 <div class="card"><h3>What's the difference between credit packs, subscriptions, and subscription tiers?</h3><p>Credit packs and subscriptions both give you credits to spend the same way, but they work differently. A one-time credit pack is pay-as-you-go: no recurring charge and credits never expire, but finished audio/video is kept for only 48 hours (download it promptly), and packs don't include voice cloning. A monthly subscription bills automatically each cycle, delivers a set number of credits every month, keeps your finished files for 30 days, and is the only way to unlock voice cloning. Each cycle's subscription credits are only good until your next renewal — any left unused are replaced (not added to) by the new cycle's amount, so they don't accumulate over time; use them within the month you get them. One-time pack credits (and anything already in your account) never expire, and they're always spent last: every generation draws from your subscription credits first, so if you've also bought a pack, those permanent credits stay untouched until that cycle's subscription allowance runs out.</p><p>Subscriptions come in a few tiers — see current names, prices, and numbers on our <a href="/pricing">Pricing page</a> — that differ in monthly credits and <strong>voice slots</strong> (how many named cloned voices you can keep saved at once, ready to reuse across projects — a slot frees up again if you delete a voice). Some plans may also include a <strong>monthly cloning allowance</strong> (a cap on how many brand-new voices you can clone during a billing cycle); if a plan has one, it is shown on that plan's card on the Pricing page. A higher tier costs more but gives you more. You can subscribe from the <strong>➕ Buy</strong> menu or the <a href="/pricing">Pricing page</a>, and cancel any time from your <a href="/account">Account</a> page — you keep access until the end of the period you already paid for.</p></div>
